WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.980
Detection engineering is the disciplined process of designing, testing, deploying, tuning, maintaining, and eventually retiring security detections.

2
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.240
A detection is more than a search query.

3
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:19.740
It connects a meaningful use case to available evidence, clear logic, operating assumptions, investigation guidance, and an accountable owner.

4
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.780
In OT, that discipline must account for physical processes.

5
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:32.040
A network event may involve a controller, HMI, engineering workstation, or remote site whose availability affects production or safety.

6
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:37.340
The same technical behavior can be normal during maintenance and concerning during steady operation.

7
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:44.740
Generic IT detections often emphasize users, endpoints, and rapidly changing applications.

8
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:54.920
OT detection also considers industrial protocols, long-lived assets, predictable communication, process state, engineering authority, and architecture.

9
00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:02.060
Some systems produce limited logs, and active testing that is routine in IT may be inappropriate near sensitive equipment.

10
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:09.300
Safety, reliability, availability, and process integrity shape both detection and response.

11
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.800
A high-confidence alert does not automatically justify isolating an asset.

12
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:20.300
Removing a controller, operator view, or communications path could create a larger operational problem.

13
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.520
Runbooks should identify which actions require operations or engineering approval.

14
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.440
Good OT detections support defenders without disrupting operations.

15
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:40.460
They use passive or existing telemetry where possible, enrich alerts with asset and process context, and explain the condition in terms an analyst can investigate.

16
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.720
They also document blind spots so confidence is not overstated.

17
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.040
The goal is trustworthy, actionable visibility.

18
00:01:48.140 --> 00:02:00.940
Detection engineering turns telemetry and industrial knowledge into repeatable decisions, then improves those decisions as equipment, threats, architecture, and operations change.
